{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Systems Theory History "}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you discuss the theory of systems history."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understands systems theories, business processes and basic concepts on IT. Create a map of processes that allows identifying areas in an information system, using IT tools to generate reports based on the company's needs. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.   Exchanges simple information on IT concepts, systems theory, and diagrams of processes."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Connectors"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use these words to connect ideas and sentences. They help you provide more information."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The most common connectors are:  <span class=\"strong\">and</span>,<span class=\"strong\"> but</span>, </span>or</span>, and <span class=\"strong\"> so</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">and </span> to join two sentences or ideas, adding more information. For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><li> Systems theorists research life systems <span class=\"strong\">and </span>use the information to solve problems. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">or</span> to mention possibilities and give options. Fot example: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><li>A system consists of attributes  <span class=\"strong\">or</span>  qualities."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">but</span> to contrast information and to give surprising or different information. For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><li>\tSystems theorists consider philosophy theories <span class=\"strong\">but</span>, does it take into account science?</li>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use  <span class=\"strong\">so</span> to talk about consequences and results, for example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><li>Systems theory is an interdisciplinary study, <span class=\"strong\">so</span> it has many different perspectives."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We record, store, and distribute algorithmic expressions."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Thank you Carol, but I have another question. What do you know about the history of systems theory?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "As the model of electrical circuits appeared along with other systems, so did new software applications and computing programs."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Present Tense - Affirmative Form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the<span class=\"strong\"> simple present </span>to talk about general habits, present facts, and repetitive actions. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In <span class=\"strong\">simple present</span> you use the base form of the verb to make an affirmative statement. For example: <br><br>  <div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"italic\">correct: Theorists <span class=\"strong\">work </span> with philosophers to understand systems. <br/>Incorrect:\tTheorists to work with philosophers to understand systems.</span></div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use just the base form to make affirmative statements. Also, remember the structure: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\">Subject + verb in base form + complement <br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">study  </span>computing and software.<br> I <span class=\"strong\">think </span> theorists need to emphasize systems' functions.</span></div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take into account when you make an affirmative statement and you are referring to a third person (he, she, it), that you have to add S at the end of the verb:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If the verb ends in s, z, ch, sh, or x you add ES:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> <span class=\"italic\">  - fix: fixes   - catch: catches  - finish: finishes"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If the verb ends in consonant + y, you remove the Y and add IES:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> <span class=\"italic\">  -study: studies   -imply: implies  - try: tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If the verbs ends in vowel + y, you just add S as the general rule:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> <span class=\"italic\">  -play: plays  \u2013 stay: stays"}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are some irregular verbs with no specific rule to form the conjugation of the third person, those verbs are: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> <span class=\"italic\"> -have: has    -go: goes  -do: does"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Keep in mind that the third person can be represented by personal pronouns or proper nouns, such as place names or peoples' names, for example: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> <span class=\"italic\">  Caroline <span class=\"strong\">plays</span> with different computer programs.<br>She <span class=\"strong\">plays </span> with different computer programs..</span></div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> <span class=\"italic\">  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We record, store, and distribute algorithmic expressions. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I need to write about the history of systems theory."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "feedback "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "Information for improvement"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Feedback is very important for the company."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "data "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "information, statistics"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Processing extracts important patterns from the data."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "basic "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "relating to something fundamental"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have some basic questions about the history of systems theory. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "view "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "perspective"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: It has two points of view."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "common "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something usual, frequent, or average"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: Identifying common patterns in a variety of systems for a unified theory. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "capture "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to obtain"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The input ca